  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Overview
    
    The Abys∴uina was a catastrophic thermal collapse in the deep fire-mines beneath Nightfall Shelf, the Nightshelf's primary settlement, during the Frozen Peace. Cascading failures in two interdependent systems — the Veil∴Glow, an aurora-channeling technique designed to cool deep-core pressure, and the Fissure∴Aurora, a controlled ice-fracturing method intended to vent excess heat — sealed the volcanic core's only relief points. The resulting steam surge flooded the Lower Galleries and adjacent tunnel networks, killing hundreds and destabilizing the geothermal veins that powered Nightshelf infrastructure.
    
    ## Mechanism and Casualties
    
    The Veil∴Glow's aurora-channeling threads failed first; the Fissure∴Aurora's fractures then sealed, trapping superheated pressure with no outlet. Steam moved upward through the tunnels faster than evacuation could proceed. The initial surge killed those in the Lower Galleries. In the hours that followed, volcanic veins went cold in sequence — third-depth forges, then relay stations, then the outer-tunnel heating network — and fire-keepers froze at their posts.
    
    The casualty figure is contested. Administrative ice from the period records approximately three hundred thermal signatures ceasing in the initial collapse zone. Nightshelf fable tradition, which attributes the disaster to the Berg's retribution against practitioners of Shawl☽ Sun — a fire-memory magic allegedly used to burn away sealed warnings in the deep ice — inflates the toll to one thousand. Neither figure accounts for the secondary deaths from cold exposure as the heating network failed. I have not found a comprehensive count in the ice, and I doubt one exists.
    
    ## Aftermath
    
    Surface colonies, fearing the Berg's structural destabilization, suspended crystal-shipments to the Nightshelf — a breach of the Flipper Accord, the trade agreement binding Aurora Stack and Nightfall Shelf, that transformed a mining disaster into a factional crisis. The Nightshelf was left rationing fire-cores with no external resupply. Evacuations continued for years.
    
    Shadow-Broker Nyla, then coordinator of Nightshelf intelligence operations, directed evacuation routing. The record is clear that her choices determined who survived. Nyla has not spoken publicly about her criteria. Foedus∴silenti, the silence-law originally binding miners to secrecy regarding deep-cavern findings, was invoked to suppress inquiry.
    
    The disaster's legal consequences included amendments to Iudicium∴culum, the prosecutorial statute originally ratified after orca infiltration of the Nightshelf settlement ☽'slew Nisaemesius~, broadening its scope to address negligence-born crises.
    
    ## Legacy
    
    The Abys∴uina is commemorated through at least six Nightshelf legal instruments, including Foedus∴silenti, Echo∴eliquiae, and Mandatum∴ccord. Its material consequences — collapsed geothermal veins, abandoned tunnel sections, unreliable fire-core supply — remain ongoing. The Lower Galleries are sealed. The ice-memory at those depths is, by all accounts, exceptionally clear. I have not been granted access.
