  annotation "note_1771582968197_0", anchor: "approximately three hundred thermal signatures ceasing in the initial collapse zone", text: "Three hundred. The administrative ice at comparable depths does not round — I have read cessation logs from the Rofundis∴rupt precise to single digits. Either someone aggregated the raw records before freezing them, or the number was composed afterward. The fable tradition's thousand is liturgy. Three hundred may also be liturgy in a more respectable coat.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771582968197_1", anchor: "Foedus∴silenti, the silence-law originally binding miners to secrecy regarding deep-cavern findings, was invoked to suppress inquiry", text: "A law designed to conceal what the mines contain, repurposed to conceal what the mines' coordinator decided. The main text names Nyla's role; the silence-law ensures no one may ask the question the main text implies. I wrote in my Foedus∴silenti annotation that the Accord's secret renegotiations were not anomalies but the system working as designed. This is also the system working as designed. Foedus∴silenti makes no distinction between secrets that protect the colony and secrets that protect the person invoking it. That ambiguity is not a flaw. It is the law's entire architecture.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771582968197_2", anchor: "two interdependent systems", text: "Interdependent by the time of the collapse. But Fissure∴Aurora's origin account claims independent development — a claim I questioned in that entry. If these were designed as a coupled system, this failure mode is negligence. If they became coupled through undocumented integration, it is something the silence-law was built to bury.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
